---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<Base title="Going digital" description="Sick notes, e-prescriptions, electronic patient records and more: how Gemeinschaftspraxis Immensen is going digital step by step.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="Going digital" title="Going digital, step by step" lead="Electronic sick notes, e-prescriptions, electronic patient records – and what comes next." />

  <article class="narrow prose">
    <p>
      Compared with many other countries, Germany’s healthcare system is far behind when it comes to digitalisation. Data protection rules,
      bureaucracy and many other factors have contributed to this.
    </p>
    <p>
      In future, however, nobody in healthcare will be able to avoid going digital – and that includes you as a patient. With fewer and fewer
      staff available, new ways of communicating are needed. Not every option suits everyone, but digital solutions work well for many patients.
    </p>

    <h2>eAU, e-prescriptions, ePA …</h2>
    <p>
      Lawmakers, health insurers and more and more patients want healthcare to become more digital, with quick access to health data. We see
      this development with a critical eye – but it also offers many opportunities.
    </p>
    <p>We are gradually digitalising individual processes at our practice, hopefully making them simpler, so you can get to your data easily.</p>

    <h2>Already available</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={site.bookingUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Online appointment booking</a> via our provider T2med</li>
      <li>Video consultations (also booked online)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>On our agenda</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A patient app for communicating with the practice</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Until all of this is set up and running, there will probably be days when things don’t run entirely smoothly. Thank you in advance for
      your understanding!
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
